    "shares_action_with": {
      "routes": [
        "GET /contacts/{contact_id}"
      ],
      "reason": "both answer with one contact and differ only in how it is named -- by its own id, or by the conversation it is on. K1's criterion asks whether the permission needs granting separately, and there is no operator who may look a customer up by id but not by conversation: it is the same fact reached two ways. So they share `contact.read` and pay the K1 second-class cost -- `control-plane-parity.md` §6.4 停用与 purge asks for 「不同 resource action、不同 route 和不同测试集合」, and the 'different action' half of it is not delivered for this pair, route and tests are still two. Named here per ADR-0048 二.1"
